  "term": "FTT",
  "definition": "FTT (failure to thrive), in child development, is a state of undernutrition in which a child cannot maintain the expected growth velocity for age and sex on growth charts, impairing normal physical growth. The packet also distinguishes organic FTT, which involves an underlying medical condition, from nonorganic FTT, which does not.",
